A||N||9||mrtgman||Have electric door lock question...||||1||
Z||000000||mrtgman||07-16-2001||02:26 PM||||I had an alarm system installed the other day in my 86 gt. I have always had to push the lock button on the door 2 or 3 times to get it to lock and unlock all the way. now with the alarm it still doe not lock on the first try. Does anyone have any ideas? I tried wd40 in the locks etc..||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||07-16-2001||03:14 PM||||If you have removed the door pannel and lubricated all parts and still no luck you will need new power door lock actuators cause over the years they have become weak.<P>very normal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrtgman||07-16-2001||03:21 PM||||How do I remove the door panel to lubricate?||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||07-16-2001||03:31 PM||||Plus.  The door lock system is obviously old.  The grommet on the end of the rod that comes out of the servo is probably worn out.  I reinforced the grommet, along with lubing everything, in mine and it locks and unlocks with ONE touch of the button now.  Watch the movement of the linkage and you'll see where the slop is.  Check to see if the servo is loose too.  There only riveted in.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-16-2001||03:41 PM||||if you have manual windows, u have to pull out the 'C' clip to remove handle. Pop out the little covers in the handle/armrest and take out the large (#3) phillips screws. then use a wide blade screwdriver or stiff putty knife between the door and the upolstery panel to pry it away on the sides and bottom. lift it up slightly so rubber window seal clears edge at top and its off. spray everything down with cleaner like 409/fantastic and wipe all the crud off you can see. then spray everything with lubricant, white lithium, silicone, WD40 or whatever. work the locks a few times to make sure its working ok, then if it is, put it back reverse order.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrtgman||07-16-2001||04:29 PM||||Thanks all! I'll try it this weekend.||||reg||7
Z||000006||formula2||07-16-2001||04:50 PM||||I have the same problem..<BR>But with power windows.how do I remove the door panel????????||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrtgman||07-16-2001||05:41 PM||||I have power windows as well.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rodrv6||07-16-2001||06:39 PM||||The door panel comes off the same way for power windows---except of course, there is no window crank to remove  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT-maniac||07-17-2001||09:26 PM||||Just run a screwdriver between the panel and the door frame until you hit one of the fasteners then carefully pry the fastener away from the door. Try to keep the fastener attached to the panel to avoid stripping out the hole it attaches to in the panel.<BR>BTW I just replaced a door lock actuator in my car as mine didn't work at all. Expensive part but easy to do if you take the door skin off.||||reg||1
